-- title:
--   Changing the q-th root of unity conjugates level automorphisms diagonally
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $q$ a prime, $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ a divisor of $M'$. Let $\xi,\xi'\in L$ both be primitive $q$-th roots of unity, let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$ (via $\ell_g\mid M'\mid q^2M'$), and let $K$ be any intermediate field of $L\subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$. The assertion is that there exists a single $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ξ' q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ K τ` there is $\gamma'\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with: $\gamma'\in\Gamma(q)$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$; the reductions modulo $q$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ satisfy $\bar\gamma'=\mathrm{diag}(1,d)\,\bar\gamma\,\mathrm{diag}(1,d)^{-1}$; and `IsLevelAutAt L q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ' K τ` holds. Here `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ K τ` says: for every weight $k\in\mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ generated by $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ — the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the elements of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ whose lower-right unit lies in $H_1$ — all integral power series $p_f,p_g$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[X]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at width $1$, with the Laurent series of $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ nonzero, every $x\in K$ whose image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ is the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the quotient of the Laurent series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the identity $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot\bigl(g\mid_k \nu_q(\gamma)\bigr)^{\wedge}=\bigl(f\mid_k\nu_q(\gamma)\bigr)^{\wedge}$ holds in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}\mathbb{C}$, where $(\cdot)^{\wedge}$ denotes the $q$-expansion at width $1$ and $\nu_q(\gamma)=\begin{pmatrix}a&b/q\\ qc&d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is the form of Shimura's reciprocity used in the project: the level automorphism attached to $\gamma$ when the $q$-division structure is read through one primitive $q$-th root of unity is attached, after conjugation by $\mathrm{diag}(1,d)$ modulo $q$, to the reading through any other primitive $q$-th root, uniformly in $\gamma$ and $\tau$. It is the variant for the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-guarded level group $H_1$, and feeds the auxiliary level-one and diamond-operator arguments that compare Galois actions on the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$.
